**Suggestion:** The polling interval created to track installation status is never cleared when the modal unmounts (e.g., user closes the modal mid‑install), so the interval keeps firing and attempting to update state on an unmounted component, causing memory leaks and noisy warnings in React; store the interval ID and clear it in a cleanup effect and when the install completes or fails. [resource leak]

<details>
<summary><b>Severity Level:</b> Major ⚠️</summary>

```mdx
- ⚠️ Background pollers run after modal closed, wasting network resources.
- ⚠️ React logs memory leak warnings updating unmounted InstallModal state.
- ⚠️ Repeated installs can accumulate intervals, degrading frontend performance.
```
</details>

