<details>
<summary><b>Steps of Reproduction ✅ </b></summary>

```mdx
1. Start the frontend dev server for the Next.js app and open the root page `/`, which
renders `Home` from `frontend/src/app/page.tsx:30-139`. The `Home` component conditionally
renders `InstallModal` when `selectedApp` is non-null (lines 131-136).

2. Perform a search so that `results` is populated, then click the "Install" button on any
`AppCard` (`AppCard` on lines 141-183, button on lines 166-171). This sets `selectedApp`
in `Home` and causes `<InstallModal app={selectedApp} onClose={() => setSelectedApp(null)}
/>` to render (lines 131-136).

3. In the `InstallModal` (definition at `frontend/src/app/page.tsx:204-383`), click
"Execute One-Click Install" (button on lines 310-315). This invokes `startInstall` (lines
224-250), which calls the backend `/install` endpoint and then creates a polling interval
via `const interval = setInterval(...)` on line 234 to repeatedly call
`/workflow/${workflowId}` and update `installStatus`/`step` state (lines 235-243).

4. Before the backend sets the workflow status to `'complete'` or `'failed'` (so the
`clearInterval(interval)` calls on lines 238 and 241 do not run), close the modal by
clicking the backdrop or the X button that triggers the `onClose` prop (lines 253-269),
which in `Home` sets `selectedApp` back to `null` (line 134) and unmounts `InstallModal`.
The interval created on line 234 continues firing after unmount, still calling
`setInstallStatus` and `setStep` on an unmounted component, leading to React "state update
on unmounted component" warnings in development and unnecessary background network
requests until the page is reloaded.
```
</details>
