```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@frontend/src/app/page.tsx` around lines 233 - 246, The polling interval
started with setInterval must be cleaned up on component unmount and each
network failure should be handled; change the code so the interval id is saved
to a ref (or a local variable closed over by a useEffect) and clear it in the
useEffect cleanup, wrap the axios.get(`${API_BASE}/workflow/${workflowId}`) call
inside a try/catch within the interval callback to catch network errors (on
catch: clearInterval, setError(err.message || "Network error"),
setStep('error')), and optionally use an AbortController to cancel any in-flight
request in the cleanup; ensure you still clearInterval when status is 'complete'
or 'failed' as currently done and reference setInstallStatus, setError, setStep,
workflowId, and API_BASE when making these changes.
```

</details>

